## Driver, counts and numerical scope

The three test modules load at top level, before main is defined and invoked, in workspace/import/lifecycle dependency order. Their entries execute once each. The relative fixture include is semantically correct; its missing binding is R1. Source inspection of the installed pinned Test implementation confirms that nested untyped testsets inherit the custom Capture type and finish records each child into the parent under with_testset. Capture stores pass counters rather than retaining every successful leaf. This is a source compatibility assessment, not Julia parsing or execution.

RED is precisely six structural missing-symbol assertions in the original stage. It neither constructs a basis nor establishes a numerical or allocation regression. GREEN requires eleven exact groups with prospective passing leaves 42, 6, 35, 56, 108, 53, 303, 6,236, 378, 108, 610, totaling 7,935. I independently derived these from every assertion-bearing helper, branch and loop. The general total is 7,747 + 4(M_native + M_markowitz) + P. The proposed fixed result requires M_native=25, M_markowitz=21 and P=4. Native n8 accepted nonunit orientation reaches four helper requests, alongside one seen request and twenty normalized importer requests; Markowitz reaches twenty plus one. P is the count of four dense64 retained-cache branches. These remain runtime premises, and different reached counts fail the exact per-group gate. The warm64 test also directly asserts actual cache owners and reuse. No count is an observed pass, and no output-driven change to fixtures or expectations is justified.

The driver saves raw test data in finally once main has entered, before aggregate result validation. Earlier import failures may produce logs only and remain rejected. The Python oracle enforces exact schemas, module paths, phase, integer thread/count fields, failure records, group ordering, nesting and total. Per-group validation rejects compensating changes to individual counts. Warnings/world-age text in either log are rejected. Source/thread checks do not claim complete transitive runtime loading or compiled-cache confinement.

